<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - BreederHQ"
  description="How BreederHQ collects, uses, shares and protects your data across the platform and mobile apps."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <main>
    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <p class="mb-8 rounded-md border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-gray-900">This is version 1.2.1 of the Privacy Policy, which takes effect on December 21, 2026. Until then, version 1.2 remains in effect: <a href="/legal/privacy-1-2" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,45%)] underline">read version 1.2</a>.</p>

        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> December 21, 2026 <strong>Version:</strong> 1.2.1 <strong>About this version:</strong> Version 1.2.1 corrects descriptions so that they match current practice: the seller identity check (§2.11, the identity verification row of the §4.3 table, and the sentence that follows that table); the AI-assisted contract import, document-reading, and drafting features (§§2.7, 3.1, 4.3, 4.4, 6, 9.1 and 9.3); the help search provider Voyage AI and the invoice details Scout AI can send (§§4.3 and 4.4); the analytics, advertising, session-recording, and performance-tracing tools on our websites and apps, including which of them wait for your consent (our cookie banner on our websites and web applications) and which do not, that Microsoft Clarity and Leadfeeder are no longer used, that a Global Privacy Control signal is treated as a choice to reject analytics cookies, and that session recording of error sessions is limited to the web application and the mobile app (§§1, 2.5, 2.8, 3.2, 4, 4.3, 6, 7.5, 8.4, 8.7 and 9.1); precise location (§§2.5 and 8.7); that you accept the User Agreements but accept or acknowledge this policy (§2.10); the mapping, postal-code, link-safety, and social-publishing services we use (§4.3); how long we keep records and what happens when you close your account or ask us to delete your data (§§2.9, 2.10, 6, 7.1 and 7.3); our security measures (§5.1); and where data is stored and processed, and whom to contact (§§5.2, 9.4 and 9.5). It also lists in §8.7 the Identity Check categories that §2.11 refers to, and states in §§1 and 12 and the closing line that this policy applies from its effective date without acceptance and that using the Services is not consent to any use for which the law requires separate consent. §12 lists the specific statements in version 1.2 that did not match our practice and says what we actually do; it does not apply retroactively, does not change the retention or deletion periods version 1.2 stated for information collected while version 1.2 was in effect (§§6 and 12), and does not limit any right or claim under version 1.2. It adds no new obligation on you.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ LLC ("BreederHQ," "we," "our," or "us") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our web application, mobile applications, Marketplace, Client Portal, our websites (including our marketing website at breederhq.com), and all related services (collectively, the "Services").</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This Privacy Policy describes our practices, and it applies to everyone who uses the Services from its effective date (§12). If you do not agree with these practices, do not access or use the Services. Using the Services is not your consent to any collection or use of your information for which applicable law requires separate consent. Some features ask for consent separately before they run, such as the AI Assistant and Scout AI (§4.4), and on our websites and web applications the analytics and advertising tools described in §2.8 load only after you accept them in our cookie banner. The session recording and performance tracing described in §2.5, Vercel Web Analytics (which does not use cookies), and Google Analytics for Firebase in the mobile app currently run without asking for consent (§§2.5, 2.8 and 8.4).</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ LLC is a Kansas limited liability company.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Capitalized terms used in this Privacy Policy have the meanings given in the BreederHQ Legal Definitions Schedule, which is incorporated into this Privacy Policy by reference.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.1 Account Information</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When you create an account, we collect:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Email address (for authentication and communication);</li><li>Name (for display and identification purposes);</li><li>Password (stored securely using industry-standard one-way hashing — we cannot read your password);</li><li>Phone number (if provided, for account recovery and communication).</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.2 Business and Profile Information</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">If you register as a Provider, we may collect:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Business name and address;</li><li>Professional credentials, licenses, certifications, and registry memberships;</li><li>Tax identification information (for payment processing and tax reporting);</li><li>Banking information (processed and stored by our third-party payment processor, not by BreederHQ directly).</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where you submit professional credentials, licenses, certifications, or supporting documents, we display the information you submit on your profile or listings as you direct, and we retain the underlying records for the duration of your account. <strong>We do not independently validate, evaluate, or vouch for the credentials or documents you submit.</strong> Our role is limited to the collection, display, retention, and (where you request) removal of the credential information and supporting documents. Validation, evaluation, and reliance on credentials is described in our Terms of Service and the applicable User Agreement.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.3 User Content</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When you use the Services, you may provide:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Photos and videos of animals;</li><li>Animal records, pedigrees, and breeding data;</li><li>Health testing results and veterinary records;</li><li>Contact information for your clients and business contacts;</li><li>Financial records, invoices, and receipt images;</li><li>Messages and communications with other users;</li><li>Documents and agreements;</li><li>Reviews and feedback.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.4 Transaction Information</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When you participate in Marketplace transactions, we collect:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Transaction details (items, amounts, dates);</li><li>Waitlist and reservation fee records;</li><li>Communication logs between Providers and Buyers;</li><li>Dispute and resolution records.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.5 Device and Technical Information</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When you use our mobile app or access the Services, we may collect:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Device type, model, and operating system version;</li><li>Browser type and version;</li><li>IP address;</li><li>Push notification tokens (to send you notifications you have enabled);</li><li>Crash reports and diagnostic information, including, for a sample of sessions in which an error occurs in the web application or the mobile app, a recording of the screens and actions around the error, made with the text on the screen masked and images and media blocked (§4.3). The Marketplace and the Client Portal do not make these recordings;</li><li>Performance traces, for a sample of page loads and page changes (currently about one in ten) in the web application, the Client Portal, the Marketplace, the mobile app, and our marketing website, whether or not an error occurs: the address of the page, how long the page and its parts took to load and respond, and the addresses of the requests the page made to our servers, sent with your browser and device details to our crash-reporting and diagnostics provider (§4.3);</li><li>App version;</li><li>Your device's precise location, only if you allow your browser to share it when a Marketplace page asks (for example, to show how far away a listing is or to find places near you). We use it to show distances and nearby results. When you use your location to search for dog parks, the Marketplace adds your coordinates to the address of the search page, so they are saved in your browser history and in any link you copy, and, if you have accepted analytics cookies, Ahrefs Web Analytics on the Marketplace (§2.8) can receive them as part of the address of the page you are viewing. Google Analytics on the Marketplace receives the page address with the search coordinates removed (§2.8). The search request the page sends to our servers also carries your coordinates, and our crash-reporting and diagnostics provider (§4.3) can receive them, in the page address and in the address of that request, as part of error reports and performance traces.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.6 Usage Information</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">We automatically collect certain information about your use of the Services:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Pages and features accessed;</li><li>Feature usage patterns and frequency;</li><li>Search queries within the platform;</li><li>Date and time of access;</li><li>Referring URLs;</li><li>Error logs for debugging and service improvement.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.7 AI Feature Interactions</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When you use AI-powered features (AI Assistant, Scout AI), we collect:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Your questions and queries submitted to AI features;</li><li>AI-generated responses;</li><li>Feedback you provide on AI responses (thumbs up/down);</li><li>Tool calls and data summaries generated during AI interactions.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This data is used to provide AI features, enforce rate limits, improve response quality, and generate aggregated usage analytics.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>AI-assisted contract import, document reading, and drafting.</strong> Some features use our AI service provider to read a document you upload. Contract import converts a contract you upload into an editable template. Other import tools read records you upload (for example, pedigrees, receipts, and health, genetic, or test reports) so their contents can be added to your records. Some features also draft text you ask for (for example, a listing description) from information in your records. When you use one of these features, the document's contents, or the information the drafting feature needs, are sent to our AI service provider as described in §4.4. Contract-import files are stored with your account as described in §6. Files uploaded to other document-reading features may be stored with your account or processed only temporarily, depending on the feature. A contract or other record can contain personal information about you and about other people, such as names, addresses, prices, payment terms, and signatures. Upload only documents you are authorized to share, and remove information the feature does not need before you upload.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Marketplace Provider listing screen.</strong> Providers may not offer animals for sale on the Marketplace. To enforce that rule, our AI service provider reads the buyer-facing text of each of the Provider's Marketplace listings (title, category and subcategory, service type, summary, description, price, duration, availability, priced items, search description, and keywords), including listings that are still unpublished drafts, together with the Provider's public business name, business description, and service area, when a Provider registers, creates, edits, or publishes a listing, or edits its public profile. This is a platform safety check that protects buyers, not an AI feature you choose to use. It runs for every Provider, whether or not the Provider's organization has turned off AI features or agreed to AI use. Section 4.4 describes what is sent and what the screen does with the result.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.8 Cookies and Similar Technologies</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">We, and the companies whose tools we use, use cookies and similar tracking technologies (such as scripts, pixels, browser storage, and, in our mobile app, analytics software built into the app) to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Maintain your session and authentication state;</li><li>Remember your preferences and settings;</li><li>Analyze usage patterns and improve the Services;</li><li>Measure our advertising, including whether a visit or sign-up came from an ad we ran;</li><li>Provide security features.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Analytics, advertising, and session-recording tools.</strong> The tools below run on the pages and in the apps named. On our websites and web applications, a cookie banner asks you to accept or reject analytics cookies. Google Analytics, Ahrefs Web Analytics, the company lookup described below, and the advertising and tag-management tools listed last load only after you accept. Until you choose, and if you reject, none of them loads. Your choice is stored in a cookie on breederhq.com and applies across our websites and web applications. Vercel Web Analytics, Google Analytics for Firebase in the mobile app, and the crash-reporting provider's session recording and performance tracing (§2.5) do not wait for your consent.</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> (Google LLC), on our marketing website, the account sign-up pages (accounts.breederhq.com), the web application (app.breederhq.com), the Marketplace, and our demonstration site, after you accept. It records the pages you view and events such as creating an account or starting a free trial, with a cookie identifier that is carried from one of these sites to the next, and it lets us measure whether a visit or sign-up came from a Google ad. On the Marketplace and the account sign-up pages, the page address it receives has its search parameters removed, except a short list of advertising-campaign, sign-up-source and cross-site visit-identifier parameters.</li><li><strong>Ahrefs Web Analytics</strong>, on our marketing website and the Marketplace, after you accept, and <strong>Vercel Web Analytics</strong>, on our marketing website, which does not use cookies and runs without waiting for your choice. They count visits and the pages viewed.</li><li><strong>Company lookup by IP address.</strong> On the pricing and contact pages of our marketing website, after you accept, we look up the company that owns the network your visit came from, using your IP address.</li><li><strong>Google Analytics for Firebase</strong> (Google LLC), in our mobile app for iOS and Android. It records the screens you open; events the app sends, such as when you customize or reset the app's navigation and when a link opens the app (with the link's path, which can include a record number, and details of how the app handled the link, such as whether you were signed in); and events the Firebase software records on its own, such as the first time the app is opened and the start of each session. It sends them with an identifier for your installation of the app, your device model, operating system, and app version, your IP address, from which Google derives an approximate location, and, where your device makes one available to apps, your device's advertising identifier.</li><li><strong>Advertising and tag-management tools.</strong> Our marketing website is built to load Google Tag Manager, the Meta Pixel (Meta Platforms, Inc.), the LinkedIn Insight Tag (LinkedIn Corporation), and the X (formerly Twitter) pixel (X Corp.) when we turn them on. When one is on, it loads only after you accept analytics cookies, and lets its company record your visit, connect it with identifiers that company holds about you, and use it to measure and target advertising, including on its own platform.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">These companies use what they collect under their own privacy policies, and some use it for their own purposes, including advertising. Our crash-reporting provider also records a sample of sessions in which an error occurs and traces the performance of a sample of page loads, as described in §2.5 and §4.3; neither waits for your consent. The session recordings are made only in the web application and the mobile app.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Your choices.</strong> You can change your answer at any time with the "Your Privacy Choices" link on our marketing website, the web application, the Marketplace, the Client Portal, and our demonstration site; the same answer applies to the account sign-up pages, which have no link of their own. If you accepted and then reject, we delete the Google Analytics cookies and the tools stop. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, our websites and web applications treat it as a choice to reject analytics cookies: they do not show the banner and do not load those tools. You can also block or delete cookies through your browser settings, use browser extensions that block these tools, and use the opt-out tools these companies offer. Blocking cookies that keep you signed in may limit functionality of the Services; blocking the tools listed above does not. The mobile app does not currently offer a setting that turns off Google Analytics for Firebase; your device's settings may let you reset or limit the use of its advertising identifier.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.9 Credential Attestation Records</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When you attest to a professional credential through the Services, we record metadata about the attestation: the date and time you submitted the attestation, the text of the attestation as you accepted it (including the version of that text), your account identifier, your IP address, and your user-agent string. We retain these records for the duration of your account and, after account termination, for as long as we need them for legal, audit, and dispute-response purposes.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.10 Legal Acceptance Records</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When you accept any User Agreement (including the Terms of Service, Acceptable Use Policy, Provider Agreement, Buyer Terms, Marketplace Transaction Terms, or Legal Definitions Schedule), or accept or acknowledge a version of this Privacy Policy, we record metadata about the acceptance or acknowledgment: its date and time, the version of the document, your account identifier, your IP address, your user-agent string, and the surface and flow through which you gave it. We retain these records for the duration of your account and, after account termination, for as long as we need them for legal, audit, and dispute-response purposes.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.11 Identity Verification (Stripe Identity)</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>The check is required to publish.</strong> Before a service provider's listings are made public on the Marketplace, and, from the date BreederHQ applies the same requirement to them, before a breeder's storefront and its listings are made public, BreederHQ requires the individual it designates for the Provider's account (currently the account's owner, or the Provider if the Provider is an individual) to pass an identity check performed by our Third-Party Identity Verification Provider, currently Stripe Identity, operated by Stripe, Inc. (the "Identity Check"). Where the requirement applies, it is not optional for anyone who newly publishes on the Marketplace. Some listings, storefronts, and services that were already public before the requirement applied to them may remain public without a passed check unless BreederHQ withdraws them.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>What you submit, and what Stripe does with it.</strong> During the Identity Check, you submit an image of a government-issued photo identification document and a live photo of your face directly to Stripe. Stripe reads the details printed on your document and compares your live photo with the photo on your document, which may involve biometric information, under Stripe's own terms, privacy policy, and procedures. Stripe performs the Identity Check on our behalf. To the extent Stripe's terms and privacy policy permit, Stripe may also process Identity Check data for its own purposes, such as fraud prevention, security, and compliance with law; for those uses Stripe acts on its own behalf, and Stripe's privacy policy governs them.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>What our systems receive and store.</strong> When we start an Identity Check, we send Stripe an internal reference to your account so that the result can be matched to it. Our systems then receive from Stripe the status of the check (for example, that it passed, did not pass, or needs more information from you) and a Stripe-generated session identifier. We store the session identifier, the status, and, for a check that passes, the date of that result. We use this information to decide whether the Provider's listings, storefront, or services may be published, to display the Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough indicator under §2.6 of the Terms of Service, and to tell you when a check needs your attention. Where a check does not pass, Stripe also gives a reason (for example, that a document had expired). We read that reason to tell you why the check did not pass, in the Services or in an email we send you. It may also be recorded for a limited time in our server operational logs, which we keep for thirty (30) days, and in error reports sent to our crash-reporting and diagnostics provider (§4.3), but we do not store it with your account's identity-check status.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>The images and details you submit to Stripe.</strong> Our systems do not request, download, or store your identification document image, your live photo, or the personal details Stripe reads from your document. Stripe holds them and retains them under its own policies, unless BreederHQ asks Stripe to delete them sooner. While Stripe holds them, Stripe's own tools make the submitted images and details viewable to BreederHQ, as the business that requested the check. BreederHQ does not copy them into its own systems.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Categories of information.</strong> For purposes of the California categories listed in §8.7, the Identity Check also involves audio, electronic, visual, or similar information (the live photo and the identification document image) and sensitive personal information (government-issued identification information, including any driver's license, state identification card, or passport number the document shows, and biometric information used to confirm identity). These are collected through Stripe as described in this Section and are not stored in BreederHQ's systems.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">See Stripe's privacy policy at stripe.com/privacy for details on Stripe's handling of your identification data.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">We use the information we collect to:</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.1 Provide and Operate the Services</h3>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Create and manage your account;</li><li>Authenticate your identity and maintain session security;</li><li>Process transactions and facilitate Marketplace activity;</li><li>Enable communication between Providers and Buyers;</li><li>Display your listings and profile information as directed by you;</li><li>Provide AI-powered features (AI Assistant and Scout) that answer questions about your data and the platform;</li><li>Provide AI-assisted contract import, document reading, and drafting features when you use them (§2.7).</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.2 Improve and Develop the Services</h3>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Analyze usage patterns to improve features and user experience;</li><li>Identify and fix technical issues through crash analytics and error logging;</li><li>Develop new features and functionality;</li><li>Conduct internal research and analytics;</li><li>Measure how well our advertising works, using the tools described in §2.8;</li><li>Improve AI response quality through aggregated analysis of query patterns.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.3 Communicate With You</h3>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Send push notifications you have enabled;</li><li>Send transactional emails (account verification, password resets, transaction confirmations);</li><li>Send service announcements and updates;</li><li>Respond to your support requests and inquiries.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.4 Safety and Security</h3>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Detect, prevent, and investigate fraud, abuse, and policy violations;</li><li>Monitor for unauthorized access or suspicious activity;</li><li>Enforce our Terms of Service and other policies;</li><li>Respond to Credential Disputes under §8.4 of the Acceptable Use Policy;</li><li>Comply with legal obligations.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.5 Payment Processing</h3>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Process payments through our third-party payment processor;</li><li>Issue tax reporting documents as required by law (e.g., IRS Form 1099-K);</li><li>Manage subscription billing.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">4. How We Share Your Information</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>We do not sell your personal information for money.</strong> The analytics and advertising tools on our websites and apps are described in §2.8, and what they mean under California law is described in §8.4. We may share your information in the following circumstances:</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.1 With Your Consent</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When you explicitly authorize sharing, such as publishing a Marketplace listing or sharing information through the Client Portal.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.2 Marketplace and Client Portal</h3>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li><strong>Marketplace listings:</strong> Information you include in a listing (animal or service descriptions, photos, pricing, Provider profile, credential attestations and uploaded supporting documents) is publicly visible to Marketplace visitors;</li><li><strong>Client Portal:</strong> Information you choose to share with your clients through the portal is accessible to those clients;</li><li><strong>Messages:</strong> Communications sent through the platform messaging system are accessible to the intended recipients.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.3 Service Providers</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">We share information with third-party vendors who help us operate the Services:</p>
        <div class="mb-6 overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm text-gray-700"><thead><tr><th class="border-b border-gray-300 py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Service Category</th><th class="border-b border-gray-300 py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Purpose</th><th class="border-b border-gray-300 py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Data Shared</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Payment Processing</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Processing transactions and payouts</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Transaction data, banking info, tax ID</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Identity Verification</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Identity Check required before Marketplace content is newly published, where that requirement applies (§2.11) (Stripe Identity); Stripe may also use this data for its own purposes (see §2.11)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Government identification document image, live photo, and document details, submitted by the individual directly to Stripe; any biometric information created by Stripe's facial comparison; an internal account reference sent by BreederHQ</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Cloud Hosting and Storage</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Data hosting and infrastructure</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">All platform data (encrypted)</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Push Notification Services</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Mobile push notifications</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Device tokens, notification content</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Crash Reporting and Diagnostics (Sentry)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Application stability and performance monitoring; for a sample of sessions in which an error occurs, in the web application and the mobile app, a recording of the session around the error, made with the text on the screen masked and images and media blocked; for a sample of page loads, performance traces (§2.5)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Device info, IP address, crash logs, error details, those session recordings (which include the pages visited, clicks, and the layout of the screens), and performance traces (page and request addresses, which for a dog park search by your location include your coordinates, §2.5, and load and response times)</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Analytics and Advertising</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Measuring use of our websites and apps, and measuring and targeting advertising, using the tools named in §2.8</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Pages viewed (for Ahrefs Web Analytics, the full page address, which for a dog park search by your location includes your coordinates, §2.5; for Google Analytics on the Marketplace and the account sign-up pages, the page address with search parameters removed except a short list of campaign, sign-up-source and cross-site identifier parameters, §2.8), events (such as account creation or the start of a free trial), cookie and device identifiers, IP address, referring pages, and ad-click identifiers; for Google Analytics for Firebase in the mobile app, the screens opened, app events, an app-installation identifier, device details, and, where available, the device's advertising identifier</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Email Delivery Services</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Transactional email delivery</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Email addresses, email content</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">AI Processing (Anthropic)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">AI Assistant and Scout AI features; AI-assisted contract import, document reading, and drafting; screening Provider Marketplace listings for animals offered for sale</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Your queries and relevant data summaries; documents you upload for import or reading, or text converted from them; information a drafting feature needs; the buyer-facing text of a Provider's Marketplace listings, including unpublished drafts, and the Provider's public business name, business description, and service area (see Section 4.4)</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">AI Search (Voyage AI)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Help Center search, including the help-article searches the AI Assistant and Scout AI run to answer your questions (see Section 4.4)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">The text of your search, or search text the AI Assistant or Scout AI builds from your question and earlier questions in the same conversation</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Mapping and Postal-Code Lookup (OpenStreetMap Nominatim; Zippopotam.us)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Turning addresses and postal codes into map locations, for example to place a profile or listing on a map, show distances, or support location searches</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Addresses, cities, and postal codes entered in profiles, listings, and searches</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Link-Safety Checking (Google Safe Browsing)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Checking links in email that arrives at the Services against lists of known unsafe websites</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Short fragments of a one-way hash of each link; not the links themselves or the rest of the message</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Social Publishing (Meta)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Publishing content to a Facebook Page or Instagram business account, only if a Provider connects one and chooses to share</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">The content the Provider chooses to share; we keep an encrypted access token for the connected account</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Public Registry Lookup</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Third-Party Registry Passthrough confirmation</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 align-top">Provider's credential identifier and issuing body name (no Personal Information beyond the attested credential data)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Each of these service providers has their own privacy policy governing their use of data. We require our service providers to protect your data and to use it, when acting for us, only for the purposes we specify. Where a provider also processes data for its own purposes, as Stripe may for the Identity Check (§2.11), that provider's own privacy policy governs that processing.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.4 AI Data Processing</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When you use AI-powered features (the AI Assistant, Scout AI, and the AI-assisted contract import, document-reading, and drafting features described in §2.7), your data is processed by our AI service provider, <strong>Anthropic</strong>, which operates the Claude AI model. Anthropic also reads Marketplace text for the Provider listing screen described below, which runs without any choice on your part to use an AI feature. Here is what you should know:</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>What data is sent to Anthropic:</strong></p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>For the AI Assistant and Scout AI: your question or query text; relevant summaries of your platform data needed to answer your query (for example, animal counts, breeding plan status, financial summaries, invoice details such as invoice numbers, amounts, balances, status, and dates, and contact information), with individual data records truncated to a maximum of 4,000 characters before transmission; and conversation history within the current chat session;</li><li>For contract import: the whole file you upload if it is a PDF, sent as uploaded, or, for other supported formats (such as a Word document or a plain-text file), the full text converted from it. Before sending converted text, we automatically remove text that looks like an email address, phone number, street address, identification or tax number, payment card number, password, or access key; this automatic removal can miss information, and nothing is removed from a PDF;</li><li>For other document-reading features: the document you upload, or its contents;</li><li>For drafting features: the information from your records that the feature needs to draft the text you ask for.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The 4,000-character truncation applies only to the AI Assistant and Scout AI. It does not apply to contract import or other document-reading features, which send the whole document.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>What data is NOT sent to Anthropic:</strong></p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Your password or authentication tokens;</li><li>Bank account and payment card details, and tax identification numbers, from your account settings or payment records (invoice and payment details such as numbers, amounts, balances, status, and dates can be sent as described above, and a document you upload for import or reading is sent with whatever it contains, subject only to the automatic removal described above for converted text);</li><li>Platform records belonging to other BreederHQ organizations (these features retrieve only your organization's records; a document you upload is sent with whatever information it contains, as described above).</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>AI search (Voyage AI).</strong> When you search the Help Center, the text of your search is sent to Voyage AI, a service that turns text into a numerical representation we use to find matching help articles. When the AI Assistant or Scout AI looks up help articles to answer you, it sends Voyage AI search text built from your question and earlier questions in the same conversation. Voyage AI receives only search text, not your other platform records, and processes it under its own terms. Help Center search does not ask for consent first, and it follows the organization setting described under "Your controls" below.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Marketplace Provider listing screen.</strong> Providers may not offer animals for sale on the Marketplace. To find listings that do, we send the following to Anthropic: the buyer-facing text of a Provider's Marketplace listings (title, category and subcategory, service type, summary, description, price, duration, availability, priced items, search description, and keywords), including listings that are still unpublished drafts, and the Provider's public business name, business description, and service area. We send it when a Provider registers, creates, edits, or publishes a listing, or edits its public profile. Anthropic's model reads that text and reports whether it offers an animal for sale. Please note:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>This screen is a platform safety check that protects buyers. It runs for every Provider, whether or not the Provider's organization has turned off AI features in Settings or agreed to use them, and the AI setting does not stop it;</li><li>We send only the text described above. It includes drafts a Provider has not yet published, because a new listing starts as a draft and the screen reads it when it is created, edited, or published. We do not send messages, private records, or documents;</li><li>The result is never an automatic decision. A finding only flags the Provider's Marketplace account for review by BreederHQ support, and notifies support. The screen does not suspend an account, unpublish a listing, or refuse a change by itself; a person decides what, if anything, to do;</li><li>Anthropic handles this text as described under "Anthropic's data handling" below.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Anthropic's data handling:</strong></p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Anthropic processes the data we send to provide these features to us;</li><li>Under our commercial agreement, Anthropic does not use data submitted through our API for training AI models;</li><li>We use documents you upload for import or reading only to provide the feature you used, to operate, secure, and support the Services, and to comply with law; we do not use them for marketing;</li><li>For details on Anthropic's data practices, see Anthropic's usage policy at anthropic.com/policies.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Your controls:</strong></p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Organization administrators can turn off AI features for their organization through Settings. Turning them off stops every feature described in this Section, other than the Marketplace Provider listing screen, from sending data to Anthropic or Voyage AI: the AI Assistant, Scout AI, the AI-assisted contract import, document-reading, and drafting features, and Help Center search, which then finds articles by keyword instead. The Marketplace Provider listing screen reads only the listing and profile text described in §4.4 (never messages, private records, or documents) and runs for every Provider;</li><li>You can delete your AI Assistant query history at any time through the Help Center;</li><li>The AI Assistant and Scout AI ask for your explicit consent before first use. Contract import, most other document-reading and drafting features, and Help Center search do not have a separate consent screen; they send a document, information, or search text only when you choose to use them. The Marketplace Provider listing screen does not depend on a consent screen or on the AI setting; it reads only the listing and profile text described above, and never messages, private records, or documents.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.5 Legal Requirements</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">We may disclose your information when required to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Comply with applicable law, regulation, legal process, or governmental request;</li><li>Enforce our Terms of Service and other agreements;</li><li>Protect the rights, safety, or property of BreederHQ, our users, or the public;</li><li>Detect, prevent, or address fraud, security, or technical issues;</li><li>Cooperate with law enforcement or regulatory investigations;</li><li>Report substantiated Credential Disputes to the issuing body or applicable licensing authorities where required by law.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.6 Business Transfers</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">If BreederHQ is involved in a merger, acquisition, reorganization, or sale of assets, your information may be transferred as part of that transaction. We will notify you of any such change and any choices you may have regarding your information.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">5. Data Storage and Security</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">We take the security of your data seriously:</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.1 Security Measures</h3>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>All data is transmitted over HTTPS using TLS encryption;</li><li>Passwords are stored using industry-standard one-way hashing (we cannot read your password);</li><li>Authentication tokens are stored in secure device storage;</li><li>Access to our production database is restricted;</li><li>We use automated tools that flag known security vulnerabilities in the software libraries we use, and automated checks, run on changes to our server code, that look for errors that could let one account reach another account's data;</li><li>Data is hosted on industry-standard cloud infrastructure with enterprise-grade physical and network security;</li><li>AI queries are transmitted to our AI service providers over encrypted connections.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.2 Data Location</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Your data is stored on servers located in the United States. AI queries are sent to our AI service provider, Anthropic, and processed on its infrastructure (§4.4).</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.3 Security Limitations</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">While we implement commercially reasonable security measures, no method of transmission over the Internet or electronic storage is 100% secure. We cannot guarantee absolute security of your data.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.4 Breach Notification</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">In the event of a data breach that affects your personal information, we will notify you in accordance with applicable data breach notification laws.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">6. Data Retention</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This section describes how we keep information collected from the effective date of this version. It does not change any retention or deletion period that version 1.2 stated for information collected while version 1.2 was in effect; §12 says how our handling of that information differs from those periods today.</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li><strong>Account data</strong> is retained while your account is open and after you close it, until it is deleted in response to a deletion request under §7.3; we may keep what the law requires or permits us to keep;</li><li><strong>Transaction records</strong> are retained for at least seven (7) years for tax and legal compliance;</li><li><strong>Credential Attestation records</strong> are retained for the duration of your account and, after account termination, for as long as we need them for legal, audit, and dispute-response purposes;</li><li><strong>Legal Acceptance records</strong> are retained for the duration of your account and, after account termination, for as long as we need them for legal, audit, and dispute-response purposes;</li><li><strong>Media files</strong> (photos, videos, uploaded supporting documents) are retained until you delete them or your account is deleted under §7.3;</li><li><strong>Contract files uploaded for import</strong>, and the drafts converted from them, are retained with your account until your account is deleted under §7.3; discarding an import draft hides it but does not delete the uploaded file, and closing your account in the Services does not delete it;</li><li><strong>Messages</strong> are retained for as long as we need them to provide the Services to the people who sent and received them;</li><li><strong>Crash reports</strong>, including session recordings, and <strong>performance traces</strong> are retained by our crash-reporting provider for a limited period;</li><li><strong>AI query logs</strong> (questions, responses, and feedback submitted to AI features) are deleted automatically ninety (90) days after they are created, or sooner if you delete them through the Help Center (§4.4) or they are deleted in response to a deletion request under §7.3;</li><li><strong>AI conversations</strong> are deleted automatically once they have had no activity for ninety (90) days, or sooner if you delete them or your account is deleted under §7.3;</li><li><strong>Usage analytics</strong> are retained in aggregated, anonymized form indefinitely;</li><li><strong>Information collected by the analytics, advertising, and session-recording tools</strong> described in §2.8 is retained by the companies that provide them, under their own settings and policies;</li><li><strong>Deleted data</strong> may persist in encrypted backups until those backups expire.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">7. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.1 Access and Portability</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You have the right to access your data through the Services while your account is open. You may request a copy of your data in a portable, machine-readable format by contacting us, including after you close your account.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.2 Correction</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You may update or correct inaccurate information in your account at any time through your account settings, or by contacting us.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.3 Deletion</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You may request deletion of your account and associated personal data by contacting us at privacy@breederhq.com.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Closing your account is not deletion.</strong> The option in your account settings to delete or close your account (labeled "Delete Account" or "Close Account," or a translation of either, depending on the version and language of the app) closes your account; it does not delete your data. Closing your account signs you out everywhere, blocks sign-in, and takes offline any Marketplace storefront that you alone own, pausing its listings. It does not take offline listings or storefronts that belong to a business account you share with others. In some cases the Services will not let you close your account, for example while you are the only owner of a business account, or while a Marketplace transaction, an unpaid invoice, or a payout connected to a storefront you own is still pending; in that case, contact us. To have your data deleted, send us a deletion request as described above.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When we carry out a deletion request:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Your profile and listings are removed from the platform;</li><li>We delete your personal data from our active systems, including contract files uploaded for import, except what we keep under the next bullet;</li><li>We may keep data that the law requires or permits us to keep (for example, transaction records for tax compliance, and Credential Attestation records and Legal Acceptance records as described in §6);</li><li>Copies in encrypted backups are deleted as those backups expire.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.4 Opt-Out of Communications</h3>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li><strong>Push notifications:</strong> Disable through your device settings or in-app notification preferences;</li><li><strong>Marketing emails:</strong> Unsubscribe using the link provided in each email;</li><li><strong>Transactional emails:</strong> Cannot be opted out of while your account is active (these are necessary for account security and service operation);</li><li><strong>AI features:</strong> Organization administrators can disable AI features through Settings; that setting does not stop the Marketplace Provider listing screen (§4.4). Individual users can delete their AI query history through the Help Center at any time.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.5 Do Not Track</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Services do not currently respond to "Do Not Track" signals from browsers. Our websites and web applications treat a Global Privacy Control signal as a choice to reject analytics cookies (§2.8). The mobile app does not respond to Global Privacy Control signals.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">8. California Privacy Rights (CCPA/CPRA)</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">If you are a California resident, you have additional rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA):</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.1 Right to Know</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You have the right to request that we disclose the categories and specific pieces of personal information we have collected about you, the categories of sources, the business purpose for collection, and the categories of third parties with whom we share your information.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.2 Right to Delete</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You have the right to request deletion of your personal information, subject to certain exceptions (such as legal compliance and transaction record-keeping).</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.3 Right to Correct</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You have the right to request correction of inaccurate personal information.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.4 Right to Opt-Out of Sale/Sharing</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>We do not sell your personal information for money.</strong> The analytics and advertising tools described in §2.8 let the companies that provide them collect information about your visits to our websites and apps, such as cookie and device identifiers, IP address, and the pages you view, and some of those companies may use it for their own advertising purposes. Under California law, making information available in that way can count as "sharing" personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising, and may count as a "sale." On our websites and web applications, those tools load only after you accept analytics cookies in our cookie banner, and our websites and web applications treat a Global Privacy Control signal as a choice to reject them (§§2.8 and 7.5). You can change your choice at any time with the "Your Privacy Choices" link on our marketing website, web application, Marketplace, Client Portal and demonstration site (§2.8). The mobile app's analytics tool does not wait for your consent and the app does not currently offer a setting that turns it off (§2.8). You can also limit collection by blocking cookies or these tools in your browser, as described in §2.8, and you may contact us at <strong>privacy@breederhq.com</strong> with any request about it.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.5 Right to Non-Discrimination</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">We will not discriminate against you for exercising your privacy rights.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.6 How to Exercise Your Rights</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">To exercise your California privacy rights, contact us at <strong>privacy@breederhq.com</strong>. We will verify your identity before processing your request. You may also designate an authorized agent to make requests on your behalf.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.7 Categories of Information Collected</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">In the preceding twelve (12) months, we may have collected the following categories of personal information:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Identifiers (name, email, IP address, and the cookie, device, app-installation, and advertising identifiers used by the tools described in §2.8);</li><li>Commercial information (transaction records, products purchased);</li><li>Internet or electronic network activity (browsing history, usage data, the interactions recorded by the analytics, advertising, and session-recording tools described in §2.8, and the session recordings and performance traces described in §2.5);</li><li>Geolocation data (approximate location derived from IP address, and precise location if you allow your browser to share it, as described in §2.5);</li><li>Professional or employment-related information (business information for Providers);</li><li>Audio, electronic, visual, or similar information (photos and videos you upload; for the Identity Check, the live photo and identification document image you submit to Stripe, which Stripe holds under its own policies and which, while Stripe holds them, Stripe's tools make viewable to BreederHQ, as described in §2.11);</li><li>Sensitive personal information: government-issued identification information (the document image and the details on it, including any driver's license, state identification card, or passport number it shows) and biometric information used to confirm identity, collected through Stripe for the Identity Check and not stored in BreederHQ's systems, as described in §2.11; and precise geolocation, only if you allow your browser to share it, used to show distances and nearby results and, for the dog park search, receivable by our analytics tools as part of the page address and by our crash-reporting and diagnostics provider as part of page and request addresses (§2.5);</li><li>Inferences drawn from the above categories.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">9. European Privacy Rights (GDPR)</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA), United Kingdom, or Switzerland, you have additional rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR):</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">9.1 Legal Basis for Processing</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">We process your personal data based on:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li><strong>Contract performance:</strong> Processing necessary to provide the Services you have requested;</li><li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> Processing necessary for our legitimate business interests (service improvement, analytics and advertising measurement using the tools described in §2.8, security, fraud prevention);</li><li><strong>Consent:</strong> Processing based on your explicit consent (the AI Assistant and Scout AI, marketing communications);</li><li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> Processing required to comply with applicable laws.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Cookies and similar tools.</strong> The legal bases above are separate from the rules on storing or reading information on your device. The law of the United Kingdom and of the EEA generally requires consent, subject to limited exceptions, before a website or app stores or reads cookies or similar information on your device for analytics, advertising, or session recording. On our websites and web applications, the analytics and advertising tools described in §2.8 that set or read such information load only after you accept analytics cookies in our cookie banner, for visitors in those places and anywhere else. The session recording and performance tracing described in §2.5, and the analytics tool in the mobile app (§2.8), do not currently ask for that consent. You can block the tools on our websites as described in §2.8; the mobile app does not currently offer a setting that turns off its analytics tool (§2.8).</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">9.2 Your GDPR Rights</h3>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li><strong>Right of access</strong> — Request a copy of your personal data;</li><li><strong>Right to rectification</strong> — Request correction of inaccurate data;</li><li><strong>Right to erasure</strong> — Request deletion of your data (subject to legal retention requirements);</li><li><strong>Right to restriction</strong> — Request limitation of processing in certain circumstances;</li><li><strong>Right to data portability</strong> — Receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format;</li><li><strong>Right to object</strong> — Object to processing based on legitimate interests, including AI data processing;</li><li><strong>Right to withdraw consent</strong> — Withdraw consent at any time where processing is based on consent.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">9.3 AI Processing and GDPR</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The AI Assistant and Scout AI use your data based on your explicit consent. You may withdraw that consent at any time by disabling AI features in your organization settings or by contacting us. When consent is withdrawn, your AI query logs can be deleted through the Help Center or upon request.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Contract import and the other document-reading and drafting features described in §2.7 process a document or information only when you choose to use them. Our legal basis for that processing is contract performance: it is necessary to provide the feature you requested. Turning off AI features in your organization settings stops contract import and the other document-reading and drafting features (§4.4). The Marketplace Provider listing screen (§4.4) is not based on consent and is not stopped by that setting. Our legal basis for it is our legitimate interest in keeping animal sales off Provider listings and protecting buyers, and a person, not the screen, decides any action on the Provider's account. You may exercise the rights in §9.2 that apply to this processing, such as the rights of access, erasure, and restriction, subject to the conditions of the GDPR, by contacting us.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">9.4 Data Transfers</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">We store and process your data on servers in the United States. If you use the Services from outside the United States, your data is transferred to the United States. Our AI service providers (Anthropic, and Voyage AI for help search) process the data we send them on their own infrastructure (§4.4).</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">9.5 Privacy Contact</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">For GDPR-related inquiries, contact us at <strong>privacy@breederhq.com</strong>.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">9.6 Supervisory Authority</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection supervisory authority.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">10. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Services are not intended for children under 13 years of age (or 16 in the EEA). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under these ages. If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has provided us with personal information, please contact us at <strong>privacy@breederhq.com</strong> and we will take steps to delete such information.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">11. Third-Party Links</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Services may contain links to third-party websites or services, including without limitation Public Registries operated by issuing bodies (such as the American Farrier's Association, American Kennel Club, Orthopedic Foundation for Animals, and state veterinary licensing boards). We are not responsible for the privacy practices of these third parties. We encourage you to review the privacy policies of any third-party websites or services you visit.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of material changes by:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Posting the updated policy on our website;</li><li>Updating the "Effective Date" at the top of this page;</li><li>Sending an email notification for significant changes.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">An updated Privacy Policy describes our practices from its effective date, and it applies to everyone who uses the Services from that date, whether or not they have accepted or acknowledged it. Continued use of the Services after that date is not your consent to any collection or use for which applicable law requires separate consent (§1).</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>What changed from version 1.2.</strong> Some statements in version 1.2 did not match our practice. This version describes our practices from its effective date. It does not apply retroactively: it does not change what version 1.2 said while it was in effect, and it does not waive, release, or limit any right you have, or any claim that arose, under version 1.2. In particular, the retention periods in §§2.9, 2.10 and 6 of this version apply to information collected from its effective date; they do not change any retention or deletion period that version 1.2 stated for information collected while version 1.2 was in effect. The differences below describe how information has actually been handled, including how information collected under version 1.2 is handled today:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li><strong>AI query logs.</strong> Version 1.2 said AI query logs were deleted automatically ninety (90) days after they were written. Automatic deletion on that schedule now runs: AI query logs, including logs written while version 1.2 was in effect, are deleted ninety (90) days after they are created (§6). You can also delete yours at any time through the Help Center, or have them deleted in response to a deletion request under §7.3.</li><li><strong>Backups and crash reports.</strong> Version 1.2 said deleted data was removed from encrypted backups within thirty (30) days and that crash reports were kept for ninety (90) days. We have not confirmed that our database and crash-reporting providers' settings match those periods. Today backup copies are deleted as the backups expire, and crash reports are kept for the period our crash-reporting provider's settings allow (§6).</li><li><strong>Credential Attestation and Legal Acceptance records.</strong> Version 1.2 said these were kept for the duration of your account and for seven (7) years after account termination. No process deletes these records at the end of a fixed period today; they are kept with the other records described in §§2.9 and 2.10.</li><li><strong>Messages.</strong> Version 1.2 said messages were kept while both parties' accounts were active. Today messages are not deleted when a party's account is closed; they are kept for as long as we need them to provide the Services to the people who sent and received them.</li><li><strong>Account data, access, and closing.</strong> Version 1.2 said account data was kept for a reasonable period after deletion and that you could access your data through the Services at any time. Closing an account does not delete its data; data is deleted when we carry out a deletion request, and in-product access ends when an account is closed, though you may still ask us for a copy (§§7.1 and 7.3).</li><li><strong>Identity check.</strong> Version 1.2 described identity verification as something a Provider could choose to complete and said BreederHQ did not receive the identification document or biometric data. The check is required to newly publish on the Marketplace where §2.11 says it applies, and while Stripe holds the images and details from a check, Stripe's tools make them viewable to BreederHQ (§2.11). BreederHQ does not store them in its own systems.</li><li><strong>AI features.</strong> Version 1.2 named only the AI Assistant and Scout AI, said payment information was not sent to our AI service provider, and did not name our AI search provider. §§2.7, 4.3 and 4.4 describe the AI document features, the invoice details Scout AI can send, Voyage AI, and the screen that reads the buyer-facing text of Providers' listings, including unpublished drafts, and the Providers' public business names, business descriptions, and service areas to find animals offered for sale and flags the account for human review, which runs whether or not AI features are turned off.</li><li><strong>Analytics and advertising.</strong> Version 1.2 said we did not share personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising and listed analytics among the processing based on consent. On our websites and web applications, the analytics and advertising tools described in §2.8 load only after you accept them in our cookie banner; the mobile app's analytics tool does not wait for consent (§§2.8, 8.4 and 9.1).</li><li><strong>Data transfers and location.</strong> Version 1.2 said that using the Services was consent to the transfer of your data to the United States, that our AI service provider processed data in the United States, and that we used Standard Contractual Clauses where required. This version makes none of those statements (§§5.2 and 9.4).</li><li><strong>Security.</strong> Version 1.2 said database access was monitored and logged and that we conducted regular security reviews and vulnerability assessments. §5.1 describes the measures we can confirm.</li></ul>
